  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1017 AM CDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nRain chances next week are abysmal until we get to Friday and into\nthe weekend, and even that's iffy. With no break in the summer\npattern, heat indices are likely to peak at least in the low 100s\nmany areas west of the Cumberland Plateau through Friday, and it\nnow appears that we may actually reach heat advisory criteria on\nTuesday, and perhaps again Wednesday. The NBM continues to hint \nat a gradual cool-down beginning next weekend as a cold front \napproaches Middle Tennessee. However, individual model solutions \ndiverge greatly when it comes to pinning down a time frame for \nthat fropa. Obviously, our next rain chances and the inevitable \ndrop in temperatures will depend largely on the timing of that \ncold front. So plenty of uncertainly remains.",
